{% macro numberField(i,key,label,help,max,step) %}
<div class="pc-field"><label for="pc-{{ i }}-{{ key }}">{{ label }}</label><input id="pc-{{ i }}-{{ key }}" data-field="{{ key }}" type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="0" max="{{ max or 10000000 }}" step="{{ step or '0.01' }}" placeholder="Not stated" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="pc-{{ i }}-{{ key }}-help"><p id="pc-{{ i }}-{{ key }}-help">{{ help }}</p></div>
{% endmacro %}
{% macro selectField(i,key,label,help) %}
<div class="pc-field"><label for="pc-{{ i }}-{{ key }}">{{ label }}</label><select id="pc-{{ i }}-{{ key }}" data-field="{{ key }}"{% if help %} aria-describedby="pc-{{ i }}-{{ key }}-help"{% endif %}>{% for value,label in proposalComparison.options[key] %}<option value="{{ value }}">{{ label }}</option>{% endfor %}</select>{% if help %}<p id="pc-{{ i }}-{{ key }}-help">{{ help }}</p>{% endif %}</div>
{% endmacro %}
<main class="proposal-page" id="proposal-comparison">
  <div class="pc-hero-shell">
    <nav class="pc-wrap pc-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Compare agency proposals</span></nav>
    <section class="pc-wrap pc-hero" aria-labelledby="pc-title">
      <div><p class="pc-eyebrow">Free tool / A clearer buying decision</p><h1 id="pc-title">Compare lead generation<br class="pc-wide-break"> agency proposals.<br><span>Know what you’re buying.</span></h1><p class="pc-lead">Put two or three proposals side by side. See the cost, what counts as a meeting and what still needs an answer.</p><div class="pc-actions"><a class="pc-button pc-button-orange" href="#pc-builder">Compare my proposals <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a><button class="pc-text-button" data-pc-example type="button" disabled>Try an example <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button></div><p class="pc-hero-note">Free. No email required. Use the details you have.</p></div>
      <aside class="pc-hero-sheet" aria-label="What the comparison helps you check"><div class="pc-sheet-top"><span>BEFORE YOU SIGN</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><p class="pc-sheet-title">The details<br>make the deal.</p><dl><div><dt>01 / COST</dt><dd>Monthly or every four weeks?</dd></div><div><dt>02 / RESULT</dt><dd>A booking or a meeting that happens?</dd></div><div><dt>03 / OWNERSHIP</dt><dd>What does your team keep?</dd></div></dl><div class="pc-sheet-foot">Compare the commitment behind the quote.</div></aside>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="pc-builder-section" id="pc-builder" aria-labelledby="pc-builder-title"><div class="pc-wrap">
    <div class="pc-section-heading"><div><p class="pc-eyebrow">01 / Your comparison</p><h2 id="pc-builder-title">Bring the quotes.<br>Make the differences clear.</h2></div><p>Start with the essentials. Open the scope checks for a fuller picture. Leave missing amounts blank; enter <strong>0</strong> when a charge is confirmed to be zero.</p></div>
    <noscript><p class="pc-alert">Enable JavaScript to compare your proposals. The worked example, definitions and questions below are available without it.</p></noscript>
    <div id="pc-tool" data-clarity-mask="true" role="group" aria-label="Agency proposal inputs">
      <div class="pc-settings"><div class="pc-field"><label for="pc-currency">Currency for every proposal</label><select id="pc-currency"><option value="USD">US dollars (USD)</option><option value="CAD">Canadian dollars (CAD)</option></select></div><div class="pc-field"><label for="pc-months">Compare over</label><select id="pc-months"><option value="1">1 month</option><option value="3" selected>3 months</option><option value="6">6 months</option><option value="12">12 months</option><option value="24">24 months</option></select></div><p>Use one currency throughout. Convert any foreign-currency quote before entering it. The tool does not apply exchange rates.</p></div>
      <p class="pc-demo-note" id="pc-demo-note" hidden><strong>Fictional example loaded.</strong> These are illustrative proposals, not agency quotes. Change any field to make the comparison yours.</p>
      <div class="pc-proposal-grid" id="pc-proposals">
      {% for letter in ['A','B','C'] %}{% set i = loop.index0 %}
        <fieldset class="pc-proposal" data-proposal="{{ i }}"{% if i == 2 %} hidden disabled{% endif %}>
          <legend>Proposal {{ letter }}</legend><div class="pc-proposal-head"><span>PROPOSAL {{ letter }}</span>{% if i == 2 %}<button type="button" id="pc-remove" class="pc-text-button" aria-label="Remove Proposal C">Remove ×</button>{% else %}<span aria-hidden="true">0{{ loop.index }}</span>{% endif %}</div>
          <div class="pc-field pc-name"><label for="pc-{{ i }}-name">Agency name <span>optional</span></label><input id="pc-{{ i }}-name" data-field="name" type="text" maxlength="70" placeholder="Proposal {{ letter }}" autocomplete="off"></div>
          <div class="pc-field-pair">{{ numberField(i,'fee','Fixed fee','Enter 0 for a proposal with only per-result charges.') }}{{ selectField(i,'billing','Billing period','Choose the period printed in the quote.') }}</div>
          <div class="pc-field-pair">{{ numberField(i,'setup','One-time setup fee','Enter 0 if no setup fee applies.') }}{{ numberField(i,'minMonths','Minimum term (months)','Enter 0 for no multi-month minimum.',36,'1') }}</div>
          {{ selectField(i,'meetingUnit','What counts as a result?','Use the definition in the proposal.') }}
          <details class="pc-scope"><summary>Scope and extra costs <span>Check what is included</span></summary><div class="pc-scope-body">
            <div class="pc-field-pair">{{ numberField(i,'extras','Other costs for the full period','Include data, tools or other fixed extras once. Enter 0 if none.') }}{{ numberField(i,'rate','Additional fee per result','Use for pay-per-result or hybrid pricing. Enter 0 if none.') }}</div>
            {{ numberField(i,'units','Result count for the full period','Use the total for your selected comparison period, not a monthly count.',1000000,'1') }}
            {{ selectField(i,'volumeType','Where does that count come from?','A target or personal scenario is not a delivery guarantee.') }}
            <fieldset class="pc-channel-fields"><legend>Work explicitly included</legend><div>{% for value,label in proposalComparison.channels %}<label><input type="checkbox" data-channel="{{ value }}">{{ label }}</label>{% endfor %}</div><p>Tick only what the proposal states. Unticked work stays unconfirmed.</p></fieldset>
            {{ selectField(i,'qualification','Buyer qualification') }}
            {{ selectField(i,'replacements','No-shows or wrong-fit results','If these have different terms, choose “Not stated” and ask about both.') }}
            {{ selectField(i,'ownership','Data and notes after the campaign') }}
            {{ selectField(i,'reporting','Reporting and handoff') }}
            {{ selectField(i,'notice','Cancellation notice','Choose “Not stated” for other terms and confirm them separately.') }}
          </div></details>
        </fieldset>
      {% endfor %}
      </div>
      <div class="pc-build-actions"><button id="pc-compare" class="pc-button pc-button-dark" type="button" disabled>Compare my proposals <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button><button id="pc-add" class="pc-text-button" type="button" disabled>+ Add a third proposal</button><button id="pc-clear" class="pc-text-button" type="button" disabled>Clear entries</button></div>
      <p id="pc-error" class="pc-alert" role="alert" hidden></p><p class="pc-input-note">The comparison runs in your browser. No account or proposal upload. Copy or print your result before leaving the page.</p>
    </div>
    <section id="pc-results" class="pc-results" aria-labelledby="pc-result-title" data-clarity-mask="true" hidden><div class="pc-result-top"><div><p class="pc-eyebrow">Your answers / Your comparison</p><h2 id="pc-result-title" tabindex="-1">Here’s what you’re comparing.</h2></div><span id="pc-result-period" class="pc-badge"></span></div><p id="pc-result-intro"></p><div id="pc-notices" class="pc-notices"></div><div id="pc-result-cards" class="pc-result-cards"></div><div id="pc-scope-comparison" class="pc-table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Proposal scope comparison"></div><div id="pc-question-cards" class="pc-question-cards"></div><div class="pc-result-tools"><button type="button" id="pc-copy" class="pc-text-button">Copy comparison and questions</button><button type="button" id="pc-print" class="pc-text-button">Print comparison</button><a href="#pc-builder">Edit my entries ↑</a></div><label for="pc-copy-text" class="sr-only">Comparison text to copy</label><textarea id="pc-copy-text" readonly hidden></textarea><p class="pc-result-limit">Costs use your inputs. Unconfirmed items remain open. Scope, execution and buyer fit still need to be assessed.</p><div class="pc-result-next"><div><h3>Get a scope you can act on.</h3><p>Bring the questions you found. We’ll show you what CallTeam would run, what your team would handle and what the investment covers.</p></div><a class="pc-button pc-button-orange" href="https://calendly.com/hello-callteam/new-meeting" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-pc-booking>Book a campaign scope call <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
    <p id="pc-status" class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="pc-example-section" id="pc-example" aria-labelledby="pc-example-title"><div class="pc-wrap pc-example-grid"><div><p class="pc-eyebrow">02 / A fictional example</p><h2 id="pc-example-title">A lower monthly fee<br>can cost more.</h2><p>For a three-month comparison, a setup charge changes the picture. Both examples below assume zero other charges.</p><button type="button" class="pc-text-button" data-pc-example disabled>Load these example proposals <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button></div><div><div class="pc-table-scroll"><table class="pc-example-table"><caption>Illustrative costs in US dollars</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Known costs</th><th scope="col">Proposal A</th><th scope="col">Proposal B</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Per calendar month</th><td>$4,000</td><td>$3,500</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Setup</th><td>$0</td><td>$2,500</td></tr><tr class="pc-total-row"><th scope="row">Three-month total</th><td>$12,000</td><td>$13,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="pc-example-foot">A: $4,000 × 3 = $12,000. B: $3,500 × 3 + $2,500 = $13,000. This explains the cost difference. It does not establish which agency will deliver better results.</p></div></div></section>

  <section aria-labelledby="pc-definitions-title"><div class="pc-wrap"><div class="pc-section-heading"><div><p class="pc-eyebrow">03 / The result behind the number</p><h2 id="pc-definitions-title">Make “a meeting”<br>mean the same thing.</h2></div><p>Compare appointment-setting proposals using a shared definition. Otherwise, a cost per meeting can describe very different outcomes.</p></div><div class="pc-definition-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Booked</h3><p>A meeting is scheduled. Confirm whether a no-show still counts and who handles rescheduling.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Attended</h3><p>The conversation takes place. Confirm who must attend and what makes the buyer a fit.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Accepted by sales</h3><p>Your team accepts the meeting against agreed criteria. Confirm the evidence, rejection window and handoff.</p></article></div><a class="pc-text-link" href="/articles/what-makes-b2b-appointment-qualified-practical-standard/">Read CallTeam’s qualified appointment standard <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></section>

  <section class="pc-proof-section" aria-labelledby="pc-proof-title"><div class="pc-wrap pc-proof-grid"><div><p class="pc-eyebrow">04 / Evidence behind a scope</p><h2 id="pc-proof-title">Ask what happened<br>after the meeting.</h2><p>CallTeam’s published SaaS campaign followed the work beyond the calendar invite. Read the buyer targeting, qualification and follow-up behind the results.</p><a class="pc-text-link" href="/case-studies/saas-demo-appointment-setting/">Read the SaaS campaign case study <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="pc-proof-data"><div><strong>11</strong><span>qualified demos booked<br>during a 90-day campaign</span></div><div><strong>2</strong><span>customers signed<br>within six months</span></div><p>Results from one past campaign. Your scope and outcome depend on your offer, market and sales follow-through.</p></div></div></section>

  <section id="pc-method" aria-labelledby="pc-method-title"><div class="pc-wrap pc-method-grid"><div><p class="pc-eyebrow">05 / How the tool works</p><h2 id="pc-method-title">Know what the<br>comparison includes.</h2><p>Built for B2B lead generation, appointment setting and outsourced SDR proposals. The calculations are visible, and the questions follow the terms you enter.</p><a class="pc-text-link" href="/articles/b2b-lead-generation-services/">Need a broader agency buying guide? <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="pc-method-list"><article><h3>One period. One currency.</h3><p>A monthly fee is multiplied by your selected months. Four-week fees use a 52-week annual basis: fee × 13 ÷ 12 × months. This estimates an equivalent cost; actual invoice dates and full billing cycles can differ. A one-time package is counted once, so confirm its scope covers your chosen period.</p></article><article><h3>Only the costs you provide.</h3><p>Known cost = fixed fee for the period + setup + other fixed costs + fee per result × entered result count. An unanswered cost stays unknown. Tax, exchange rates, internal sales costs, notice periods and future renewals are not added. Minimum-term fixed cost covers the fixed fee and setup only.</p></article><article><h3>Questions tied to the gaps.</h3><p>The tool checks unclear fees, result definitions, qualification, replacement terms, data access and handoff. It gives you up to five priority questions per proposal. It does not assess provider performance or award a winner.</p></article><article><h3>Your entries stay in this comparison.</h3><p>No document uploads or account are needed. Calculation code runs locally and does not transmit proposal values. Input and result areas are masked from session replay. Use copy or print to keep the result; it is not automatically attached to a booking.</p></article></div></div></section>

  <section class="pc-faq-section" aria-labelledby="pc-faq-title"><div class="pc-wrap pc-faq-grid"><div><p class="pc-eyebrow">06 / Before you decide</p><h2 id="pc-faq-title">Better questions.<br>A clearer commitment.</h2></div><div class="pc-faqs">{% for faq in proposalComparison.faqs %}<details><summary>{{ faq.q }}</summary><p>{{ faq.a }}</p></details>{% endfor %}</div></div></section>

  <section class="pc-next-section" aria-labelledby="pc-next-title"><div class="pc-wrap"><div class="pc-section-heading"><div><p class="pc-eyebrow">07 / Put the decision to work</p><h2 id="pc-next-title">Build the business case.<br>Then build the campaign.</h2></div><p>Take the next step that fits your decision. You can model the return, explore an approach or discuss the scope directly.</p></div><div class="pc-next-links"><a href="/b2b-lead-generation-roi-calculator/"><span>THE NUMBERS</span><strong>Calculate your campaign ROI</strong><p>Use customer value and sales assumptions to test the business case.</p><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a><a href="/b2b-outbound-campaign-planner/"><span>THE APPROACH</span><strong>See how we’d run your campaign</strong><p>Explore a starting approach for your market and buyer.</p><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a><a href="https://calendly.com/hello-callteam/new-meeting" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-pc-booking><span>THE CONVERSATION</span><strong>Book a campaign scope call</strong><p>Let’s agree on the buyers, the work and the next step.</p><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a></div><p class="pc-pricing-link">Considering CallTeam? <a href="/pricing/">See current pricing and what affects the scope.</a></p></div></section>
</main>
